{
  "name": "Publish a short video to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts and confirm it went live",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Publish a short video to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts\n\nSend one vertical video to three networks, then wait until each one says it is live. Try it first with check_only on: every check runs and nothing is posted.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Your settings** holds the video URL, the caption, the YouTube title, check_only and an optional time to publish at.\n2. **Import video** copies the video to Status 200 Uploads and waits until it is ready.\n3. The three **Publish** nodes post it, schedule it, or only check it. Each request carries an automatic Idempotency-Key, so a retry never posts twice.\n4. A post sent now is read every 30 seconds, for up to 10 minutes, until its network is done. Checks and scheduled posts are reported at once.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node `@status200uploads/n8n-nodes-status200uploads` (Settings, Community Nodes). Until n8n verifies it, it installs on self-hosted n8n only.\n2. In your Status 200 Uploads dashboard, connect TikTok, Instagram and YouTube, and create an API key on the API page.\n3. Create a **Status 200 Uploads API** credential with that key. In each Publish node choose the credential and your account. In **Publish to TikTok** choose who can see the video; in **Publish to YouTube Shorts** the video is private until you choose otherwise.\n4. Fill in **Your settings**, run once with check_only true, then set it to false.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "4cebba65-5e32-4e03-a7d3-86864fcb542d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-580, -280]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Your settings\ncheck_only true runs every check and posts nothing. Leave publish_at empty to post now, or give a date and time such as 2026-10-01 09:00 (the workflow's time zone) to schedule it.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3ab2e5ae-9054-46c5-8ed2-d9e27c3f344d",
      "name": "Note: settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Import the video\nMP4, MOV or WebM, up to 5 GB, from a public URL. The node waits up to 10 minutes until it is ready.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 240,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "dfc093a8-3516-4d1c-af4a-c4317cc18cab",
      "name": "Note: import",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [420, -180]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Publish\nOne node per network. TikTok and Instagram finish after the answer, and YouTube uploads in the background, so the next step waits for them.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "58ef9028-6d62-4a84-b501-1352499b59e0",
      "name": "Note: publish",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [680, -360]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Wait until it is live\nEach post sent now is read every 30 seconds until it is done, at most 20 times. Checks and scheduled posts skip the wait. Post: Cancel stops a scheduled post by its scheduled_post_id.",
        "height": 680,
        "width": 1180,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "c7048802-61fd-410e-9611-6af045ccd86d",
      "name": "Note: result",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [980, -360]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
